card.statement:
(a) The set of Kronecker canonical forms of all pairs obtained by perturbations of the blocks $(2,1)$ in

\begin{equation}
\mc L_m\oplus {\cal D}_n(\lambda )
\end{equation}

consists of the pairs

\begin{equation}
\mc L_{m+r} \oplus \mc D_{n-r}(\lambda ),\quad\text{in which } 0\le r\le n.
\end{equation}

(b) Each pair <<ref:cxma>> with $r>0$ is equivalent to a pair of the form

\[\begin{aligned}
&\left(
\mat{
L_m&0\\ 0&I_n},\,
\mat{
R_m&0
\\ \D_{r}(\varepsilon)^T&J_n(\lambda )}
\right)
&&\text{if }\lambda \in\mathbb C
\\
&\left(
\mat{
L_m&0\\ 0&J_n(0)},\,
\mat{
R_m&0\\ \nabla_{r}(\varepsilon)^T&I_n}
\right)
&&\text{if }\lambda =\infty
\end{aligned}\]

(which is obtained by an arbitrarily small perturbation of <<ref:bmxa>>), in which $\varepsilon$ is an arbitrary nonzero complex number.
